    "https://apply.interfolio.com/183017": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Psychiatric Nursing",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-03-10 Location: Valparaiso, Indiana Valparaiso University College of Nursing and Health Professions invites applications for the position of Assistant or Associate Professor of Psychiatric Nursing. Valparaiso University (\"Valpo\"), a community of learning grounded in the Lutheran tradition of scholarship, freedom, and faith, prepares students to lead and serve both church and society. Located one hour southeast of Chicago on a 310-acre campus, Valpo is a comprehesive university with an enrollment of over 2,500 undergraduate and graduate students. Valpo is consistently recognized as one of the best private universities in the Midwest and is located in Valparaiso, Indiana, a county seat of 40,000 residents with high quality schools and an active social community. The position is a full time, 9-month tenure-track appointment, beginning August 2026. The responsibilities of this position include teaching undergraduate/graduate courses in the BSN and DNP programs. Additional responsibilities will include working collaboratively with faculty within the CONHP and the university; providing service to the university, profession, and the practice community; and developing a research and scholarly agenda of contributions to the field. Candidates should be interested in working at a university engaged in issues in Christian higher education in the Lutheran tradition. The College of Nursing and Health Professions has programs in nursing (BSN and DNP), exercise science (BSXS), health science (BSHS), healthcare leadership (BSHL), healthcare administration (MHCA), public health (BSPH and MPH), physician assistant studies (MSPA), and occupational therapy (DrOT, OTD). The successful candidate will hold an earned doctorate in nursing, preferably Ph.D., and have three or more years of academic experience, inclusive of psychiatric/mental health nursing. The position is announced at the assistant professor level, but outstanding candidates could be considered at a higher rank with multiple years of teaching experience, an established research agenda, and scholarly accomplishments. Candidates should be interested in working at a university engaged in issues in Christian higher education in the Lutheran tradition. The College of Nursing and Health Professions has programs in nursing (BSN and DNP), exercise science (BSXS), health science (BSHS), healthcare leadership (BSHL), healthcare administration (MHCA), public health (BSPH and MPH), physician assistant studies (MSPA), and occupational therapy (DrOT, OTD). As a campus with an increasingly diverse student body, we encourage applications from individuals with a commitment to mentoring students from underrepresented communities. Please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, undergraduate and graduate transcripts, teaching statement, research statement, and contact information for three references to Interfolio at https://apply.interfolio.com/183017 . In your cover letter, please include brief statements of (a) how you might contribute to the university's distinctive mission, and (b) what experiences you have had which will enable you to mentor a diverse student body. Candidates who submit names of references should expect that the search committee will contact these references, in confidence, and that credentials will be confirmed prior to hire. Employment will require a satisfactory criminal background check. Applications will be considered until the position is filled. For specific questions or additional information about the search, contact Dr. Christina Cavinder at christina.cavinder@valpo.edu or 219.548.7797. Valparaiso University does not unlawfully discriminate and aims to employ persons of various backgrounds and experiences to develop and support its diverse community. Its entire EOE policy can be found at: http://www.valpo.edu/general-counsel/policies/equal-opportunity-policy/ .",
      "department": "Nursing"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193878": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Exercise Science",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-17 Location: Valparaiso, Indiana Valparaiso University invites applications for the position of Assistant or Associate Professor of Exercise Science, in the College of Nursing and Health Professions (CONHP). Valparaiso University (Valpo), a community of learning grounded in the Lutheran tradition of scholarship, freedom, and faith, prepares students to lead and serve both church and society. Located one hour southeast of Chicago on a 310-acre campus, Valpo is a comprehensive university with an enrolment of approximately 2,100 undergraduate and graduate students. Valpo is consistently recognized as one of the best private universities in the Midwest and has an increasingly diverse student body. This is a full-time, nine-month, tenure-track faculty appointment beginning in August 2027. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate courses in the Exercise Science program, including classroom and laboratory instruction consistent with their area of expertise. Additional responsibilities include mentoring students; collaborating with faculty across the College of Nursing and Health Professions (CONHP) and the university; participating in curriculum development, program assessment, and accreditation activities; providing service to the department, college, university, profession, and community; and developing and maintaining an active program of research and scholarship that contributes to the discipline. Candidates must hold an earned doctorate in Exercise Science, Exercise Physiology, Biomechanics, Kinesiology, or a closely related field by the appointment date. Applicants should demonstrate evidence of, or strong potential for, effective teaching, scholarly productivity, and collaborative engagement. Professional membership and/or certification through the National Strength and Conditioning Association (NSCA) and/or the American College of Sports Medicine (ACSM) is preferred. The position is advertised at the Assistant Professor rank; however, exceptional candidates with significant teaching experience, an established record of research and scholarship, and qualifications commensurate with a higher academic rank may be considered for appointment at the Associate Professor level, consistent with university policies. The College of Nursing and Health Professions has programs in nursing (BSN and DNP), exercise science (BSXS), health science (BSHS), healthcare leadership (BSHL), healthcare administration (MHA), public health (BSIPH and MPH), physician assistant studies (MSPA), and occupational therapy (DrOT, OTD). As a campus with an increasingly diverse student body, we encourage applicants with a commitment to, and experience in, mentoring students from an array of backgrounds. Please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, undergraduate and graduate transcripts, teaching statement, research statement, and contact information for three references via Interfolio at https://apply.interfolio.com/193878 In your cover letter, please include brief statements of (a) how you might contribute to the university's distinctive mission, and (b) what experiences you have had which will enable you to mentor a diverse student body. Candidates who submit names of references should expect that the search committee will contact those references in confidence and that credentials will be confirmed prior to hire. Candidates should also expect that the search committee will review their LinkedIn profile.  Employment will require a satisfactory criminal background check. Applications will be considered until the position is filled; however, applicants are encouraged to apply by October 30, 2026 for timely consideration.   For questions, contact Dr. Phrosini Samis-Smith at phrosini.samissmith@valpo.edu or 219.464.5235. Valparaiso University does not unlawfully discriminate and aims to employ persons of various backgrounds and experiences to develop and support its diverse community. Its entire EOE policy can be found at: http://www.valpo.edu/general-counsel/policies/equal-opportunity-policy/ .",
      "department": "Exercise Science"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195168": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Humanities and Ethics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06 Location: Valparaiso, Indiana Valparaiso University invites applications for the position of assistant professor, in Christ College—the Honors College (valpo.edu/christ-college). Valparaiso University (“Valpo”), a community of learning grounded in the Lutheran tradition of scholarship, freedom, and faith, prepares students to lead and serve both church and society. Located one hour southeast of Chicago on a 310-acre campus, Valpo is a comprehensive university with an enrollment of approximately 2,100 undergraduate and graduate students. Christ College, the interdisciplinary honors college of Valparaiso University, invites applications for a tenure-track position at the assistant level, beginning August 2027. The college seeks candidates from across the humanities and social sciences whose teaching and scholarship is in ethics, broadly construed: we are particularly interested in those who are interested in teaching at the intersection of ethics and technology, society, and/or health. Candidates will carry a 4/3 teaching schedule and will teach regularly in the interdisciplinary first-year program “Texts and Contexts,” which is rooted in a Great Conversations, or Transformative Texts approach. In addition to teaching, Christ College faculty conduct scholarship in their respective fields (with professional development fund support) and engage in a lively community of learning. Candidates will be in sympathy with the Lutheran mission of the University. The expected starting salary will be in the range $56,000-60,000, depending on experience. Christ College — The Honors College at Valparaiso University offers the benefits of a selective liberal arts college to Valpo’s most ambitious students. In keeping with Valpo’s mission, throughout its nearly 60-year history, the College has strived to keep alive certain vital questions, including the relationship between religious faith and the pursuit of truth. The College is an interdisciplinary academic unit with a full-time faculty of six who work closely with talented and motivated students. Christ College students represent majors from all disciplines within the College of Arts and Sciences as well as from Valpo’s three professional colleges. Emulating the Cambridge-Oxford model, students examine topics in engaging, discussion-focused seminar classes. All faculty appointments are housed in the honors college, rather than jointly appointed. For more information about the Christ College Curriculum please see: valpo.edu/christ-college/curriculum. Qualifications include: Experience teaching undergraduate classes in any field of the humanities or ethics. Must have a Ph.D. in hand (by June 2027). Excited about in-person teaching in an engaged community of learning. Experience teaching writing at the first-year level is a plus. As a campus with an increasingly diverse student body, we encourage applicants with a commitment to, and experience in, mentoring students from an array of backgrounds. Please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching statement (one page), research statement (one page), and contact information for three references to Interfolio at https://apply.interfolio.com/195168 . Candidates who submit names of references should expect that the search committee will contact these references in confidence and that credentials will be confirmed prior to hire. Employment will require a satisfactory criminal background check. Applications will be considered until the position is filled; however, applicants are encouraged to apply by November 15 for timely consideration. About the Community: Valpo is located in Valparaiso Indiana, a county seat of 35,000 residents with high quality schools and an active social community located 50 miles from downtown Chicago and only 14 miles from the beautiful Indiana Dunes National Park. Valparaiso is home to 13 city parks, over 20 miles of bike trails, and award-winning downtown gathering spaces that house year-round community events including: the Popcorn Festival, music concerts, ice skating, farmer’s markets and more. The city was built to support neighborhood activities, with most neighborhoods being within walking distance of parks, schools, and communal spaces. With the university located less than one mile from downtown, its central location within the community makes it easy for employees to enjoy the growing amenities the city has to offer. Valparaiso has been recognized as one of the top communities in Indiana and is in one of the fastest growing counties in the state. It is an area that continues to show economic growth and diversification of its residents. EOE and Nondiscrimination Policies: Valparaiso University does not unlawfully discriminate and aims to employ persons of various backgrounds and experiences to develop and support a diverse community. Its EOE policy can be found at http://www.valpo.edu/general-counsel/policies/equal-opportunity-policy/ . Successful applicants will demonstrate a commitment to cultural diversity and the ability to work with individuals or groups from diverse backgrounds. In addition to strong academic qualifications and excellence in teaching, the University highly values experience in working across cultural and other significant differences. Employment at Valparaiso University will require a satisfactory criminal background check. VALPARAISO UNIVERSITY’S DIVERSITY, EQUITY, AND INCLUSION STATEMENT Valparaiso University is a welcoming community, grounded in the Lutheran tradition, built on values of mutual respect, positive regard, freedom, and reliance on grace. We strive to boldly include all individuals and groups who contribute to the life of our campus in a mutually beneficial way. Difference is a strength and reason for celebration, and we affirm that we are most inclusive when we bring groups together to make decisions in collaborative, equitable ways. Our values do not support language or behavior that demeans members of our campus based on age, appearance, ethnicity, race, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, biological sex, disabilities (mental and physical), ideological/political positions, intellectual perspective, socio-economic status, immigration status, veteran status, and national or regional origin. Actions and behaviors based on positions or perspectives that inherently marginalize, oppress, or deny full dignity to all are not tolerated. Nothing herein shall limit academic freedom or the freedom of expression pursuant to University policy related to either. As such, we will consistently and vigilantly assess our academic and co-curricular offerings and our admissions, hiring, and promotion policies in reflection of these values.",
      "department": "Valparaiso University"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195666": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Business Analytics",
      "description": "Posted: Oct 14, 2026 Location: Valparaiso, IN Position Description The College of Business at Valparaiso University invites applications for the tenure-track Assistant Professor of Business Analytics position beginning August 2027. The primary teaching focus is our required undergraduate business statistics course. Candidates will also have the opportunity to teach other analytics courses related to their area of expertise, which could include undergraduate or graduate-level courses such as advanced business statistics, machine learning, analytic modeling,  database management, or visual effects. This tenure-track position involves teaching six courses per year (a 3-3 load), maintaining an active program of research and scholarship, and contributing to university service. We strongly prefer prior teaching experience demonstrating effectiveness in both in-person and online settings. Valparaiso University (“Valpo”) is a community of learners rooted in the Lutheran tradition of scholarship, freedom, and faith that prepares students to lead and serve both church and society. Valpo is a comprehensive liberal arts university with around 2,500 undergraduate and graduate students and is consistently recognized among the top private universities in the Midwest. Qualifications Applicants should hold a Ph.D. in business analytics or a related discipline. ABD candidates will be considered if they expect to complete their degree prior to the start date. Candidates with relevant graduate degrees and significant teaching and/or professional experience in business analytics may also be considered. This position is scheduled to start in August 2027. Application Instructions Please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching statement, research statement, and contact information for three references to Interfolio at https://apply.interfolio.com/195666 . In your cover letter, please include brief statements of (a) how you will contribute to the university’s distinctive mission and (b) your experience mentoring and preparing students for business careers. Search committee members will contact all references confidentially, and credentials will be verified prior to hire. Applications will be considered until the position is filled; however, applicants are encouraged to apply by December 15th for full consideration. About the Community Valparaiso, Indiana, is a vibrant community of 35,000 recognized as one of Indiana's top communities in one of the state's fastest-growing counties. It offers high-quality schools and an active social community. Valpo is only 50 miles from downtown Chicago and 14 miles from the beautiful Indiana Dunes National Park. It features 13 city parks, over 20 miles of bike trails, and award-winning downtown gathering spaces that host year-round community events, including the Popcorn Festival, music concerts, ice skating, farmer’s markets, and more. The city was built to support neighborhood activities, with most neighborhoods being within walking distance of parks, schools, and communal spaces. The University is located less than a mile from downtown, allowing faculty and staff to easily enjoy the city's growing cultural and social amenities. Equal Employment Opportunity and Nondiscrimination Policies Valparaiso University is an Equal Opportunity Employer (EOE) dedicated to preparing students to lead and serve in a complex world by fostering a campus community rich in varied backgrounds, viewpoints, and experiences. Our EOE policy is available at  http://www.valpo.edu/general-counsel/policies/equal-opportunity-policy/. In addition to seeking strong academic qualifications and excellence in teaching, we seek candidates who demonstrate a commitment to student success and the ability to mentor, teach, and work effectively with individuals from all walks of life. Employment at Valparaiso University will require a satisfactory criminal background check.",
      "department": "College of Business"
    }
  },
